<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Metlife lifts yr shr, div.</title>
<headline>Metlife lifts yr shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended Sept 30, 1996</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		 195	vs 156</p>
<p>    Final div (cts)	  78.5    making 130 vs 103</p>
<p>    Attrib surplus	  134	vs 106</p>
<p>    Premium income	 2,069     vs 1,669</p>
<p>    Recurring premiums   1,748     vs 1,389</p>
<p>    Single premiums	  321     vs 280</p>
<p>    Investment income	695     vs 535</p>
<p>    Marketing expenses     369     vs 313</p>
<p>    Operating expenses     269     vs 217</p>
<p>Div payable Dec 27</p>
<p>On register Dec 13</p>
<p>Full name: Metropolitan Life Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The directors have proposed a 10-for-one share split, which will translate into a 7.85 cents final dividend.</p>
<p>A once-off amount of 500 million rand has been set aside to provide additional bonuses to policy holders over the next 2-3 to mark the company's centenery in 1998.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
